§§ `C. The Director's table (C01-C04)`

-- C01, C02: table not held, the employer computes by items (1)-(5): 575 and 156. Class AMBIGUITY (reading R1): the encoding refuses.
#ASSERT `the employer deducts, given the Director's table` NOTHING EQUALS 575 -- C01
#ASSERT `the employer deducts, given the Director's table` NOTHING EQUALS 156 -- C02
-- C03: table held, its figure is deducted.
#ASSERT `the employer deducts, given the Director's table` (JUST 600) EQUALS 600 -- C03
-- C01 again at the Schedule A function (items 1-5 alone): 575.
#ASSERT `Schedule A — the tax on a month's salary of` 10_000 `in` 2026 `for` `independent: ordinary card, 2.25` `with` `independent: figures 2026` `reading` `independent: default readings` EQUALS 575

§§ `D. No card, incomplete card, additional position (D01-D08)`

#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: full month` 10_000) `given` `independent: no card` EQUALS RIGHT 4_700 -- D01
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: full month` 10_000) `given` `independent: card without other-income section` EQUALS RIGHT 4_700 -- D02
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: full month` 10_000) `given` `independent: ordinary card, 2.25` EQUALS RIGHT 575 -- D03
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: additional-position payment` 10_000) `given` `independent: declared additional position` EQUALS RIGHT 4_700 -- D04
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: full month` 100_000) `given` `independent: no card` EQUALS RIGHT 47_000 -- D05
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: full month` 3_333) `given` `independent: no card` EQUALS RIGHT 1_566.51 -- D06
#ASSERT `the withholding on` (`independent: full month` 10_000) `given` `independent: no card` `with` `independent: figures 2026` `reading` `independent: default readings` `under the direction` (`deduct at the rate` (30%)) EQUALS RIGHT 3_000 -- D07

§§ `E. Partial salary, pension, Form 0130 (E01-E14)`

GIVEN s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A payment of salary`
`independent: partial salary` s MEANS
    `independent: payment of salary` s `, part paid` s `, days` 15 `, hours a day` 4 `, hours a week` 20 `, pension` FALSE `, paid in` 2026 `, for` 2026

GIVEN s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A payment of salary`
`independent: pension` s MEANS
    `independent: payment of salary` s `, part paid` s `, days` 22 `, hours a day` 8 `, hours a week` 40 `, pension` TRUE `, paid in` 2026 `, for` 2026

#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: partial salary` 3_000) `given` `independent: ordinary card, 2.25` EQUALS RIGHT 1_410 -- E01
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: partial salary` 3_000) `given` `independent: form 0130` EQUALS RIGHT 0 -- E02
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: partial salary` 7_000) `given` `independent: form 0130` EQUALS RIGHT 156 -- E03
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: pension` 9_000) `given` `independent: ordinary card, 2.25` EQUALS RIGHT 4_230 -- E04
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: pension` 9_000) `given` `independent: form 0130` EQUALS RIGHT 435 -- E05
-- E06: a pension of 10,000 of which 5,700 is exempt: the 4,300 left is deducted at 47%: 2,021.
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: pension` (`the part of a pension of` 10_000 `from which tax is deducted, the part exempt under section 9A or 9B being` 5_700)) `given` `independent: ordinary card, 2.25` EQUALS RIGHT 2_021 -- E06
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: partial salary` 7_000) `given` `independent: form 0130 then other income` EQUALS RIGHT 3_290 -- E07
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: additional-position payment` 10_000) `given` `independent: additional position and form 0130` EQUALS RIGHT 4_700 -- E08
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: payment of salary` 3_000 `, part paid` 3_000 `, days` 22 `, hours a day` 5 `, hours a week` 25 `, pension` FALSE `, paid in` 2026 `, for` 2026) `given` `independent: ordinary card, 2.25` EQUALS RIGHT 1_410 -- E09
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: payment of salary` 10_000 `, part paid` 10_000 `, days` 20 `, hours a day` 6 `, hours a week` 30 `, pension` FALSE `, paid in` 2026 `, for` 2026) `given` `independent: ordinary card, 2.25` EQUALS RIGHT 575 -- E10
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: payment of salary` 1_000 `, part paid` 1_000 `, days` 4 `, hours a day` 6 `, hours a week` 6 `, pension` FALSE `, paid in` 2026 `, for` 2026) `given` `independent: ordinary card, 2.25` EQUALS RIGHT 470 -- E11
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: payment of salary` 10_000 `, part paid` 10_000 `, days` 18 `, hours a day` 8 `, hours a week` 40 `, pension` FALSE `, paid in` 2026 `, for` 2026) `given` `independent: ordinary card, 2.25` EQUALS RIGHT 575 -- E12
-- E13 (17 days of 8 hours: a day worker, Schedule B) is out of scope (SCOPE); no month figure is decided, so no assertion.
-- E14: 12 days of 4 hours: both "partial salary" and "day worker"; I take partial salary: 47% of 3,000 = 1,410. Class AMBIGUITY (L).
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: payment of salary` 3_000 `, part paid` 3_000 `, days` 12 `, hours a day` 4 `, hours a week` 11 `, pension` FALSE `, paid in` 2026 `, for` 2026) `given` `independent: ordinary card, 2.25` EQUALS RIGHT 1_410 -- E14

§§ `F. Part payments (F01-F02)`

GIVEN part IS A NUMBER
      s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A payment of salary`
`independent: part paid` part `of` s MEANS
    `independent: payment of salary` s `, part paid` part `, days` 22 `, hours a day` 8 `, hours a week` 40 `, pension` FALSE `, paid in` 2026 `, for` 2026

#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: part paid` 6_000 `of` 10_000) `given` `independent: ordinary card, 2.25` EQUALS RIGHT 345 -- F01a
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: part paid` 4_000 `of` 10_000) `given` `independent: ordinary card, 2.25` EQUALS RIGHT 230 -- F01b
-- F02: 287.50 exact or 288; I flagged this as an ambiguity (L): the encoding is expected to refuse (fork F3).
#ASSERT `independent: withholding` (`independent: part paid` 5_000 `of` 10_000) `given` `independent: ordinary card, 2.25` EQUALS RIGHT 287.5 -- F02

§§ `G. Bonuses (reg 4(a)) (G01-G15)`

#ASSERT `independent: bonus` 12_000 `, bankrupt` FALSE `, on salary` 10_000 EQUALS 2_364 -- G01
#ASSERT `independent: bonus` 60_000 `, bankrupt` FALSE `, on salary` 10_000 EQUALS 11_964 -- G02
#ASSERT `independent: bonus` 100_000 `, bankrupt` FALSE `, on salary` 20_000 EQUALS 32_544 -- G03
#ASSERT `independent: bonus` 6_000 `, bankrupt` FALSE `, on salary` 5_000 EQUALS 72 -- G04
#ASSERT `independent: bonus` 1_000 `, bankrupt` FALSE `, on salary` 10_000 EQUALS 156 -- G05
#ASSERT `independent: bonus` 24_000 `, bankrupt` FALSE `, on salary` 59_000 EQUALS 11_592 -- G06
#ASSERT `independent: bonus` 6_000 `, bankrupt` TRUE `, on salary` 10_000 EQUALS 1_500 -- G08
#ASSERT `independent: bonus` 100_000 `, bankrupt` TRUE `, on salary` 10_000 EQUALS 25_000 -- G09
-- G15: no salary in the month: the formula read literally gives 6,900 (L).
#ASSERT `independent: bonus` 120_000 `, bankrupt` FALSE `, on salary` 0 EQUALS 6_900 -- G15

§§ `M. Other (M01)`

-- M01: December 2026 salary paid 10 January 2027: the 2027 figures equal 2026: 575 (year assignment is an ambiguity, immaterial).
#ASSERT `the withholding on` (`independent: payment of salary` 10_000 `, part paid` 10_000 `, days` 22 `, hours a day` 8 `, hours a week` 40 `, pension` FALSE `, paid in` 2027 `, for` 2026) `given` `independent: ordinary card, 2.25` `with` (`the annual figures published for tax year` 2027) `reading` `independent: default readings` `under the direction` `no direction` EQUALS RIGHT 575 -- M01
